Sprint 1.

1. Aesthetics – How does it look?
Contrast – Text is clear and easy to read.
Alignment – Everything is lined up neatly.
Proximity – Related items are close: unrelated items have space.
Consistency – Same fonts, colours, and styles across pages.
Balance – Not too crowded or too empty.
White Space – Enough empty space around text and images.
Score (0–6): 4
Feedback:
“I think you should make sure the spacing between images is consistent within each section, so the images have even spacing around and between them. You should also make sure the text fonts and sizes are the same across sections, or, make them different across sections instead of having two sections with the same font, and the other with a different font. The colour palette is cohesive and looks nice.”

2. Functionality – Does it work?
Links – All links work and go to the right place.
Navigation – Menus and buttons take you where expected.
Scrolling – You can scroll without problems.
Page Load – No errors: all images and text appear.
Responsive – Works well on a desktop screen.
Score (0–5): 3
Feedback:
“You should add your links to your recipe pages (other html files/links) in your next sprint and make it clear that the user needs to click on the image or text of the recipe to take it to the recipe page.”

3. Usability – Is it easy to use?
Readability – Text is big enough and easy to read.
Accessibility – Clear headings, alt text for images, good contrast.
Find Info – Information is easy to find.
User Friendly – Feels welcoming and clear.
Score (0–4): 4
Feedback:
“There are clear appropriately-sized headings depending on the importance of the heading and the code in your html has alt text.”

4. Bonus Criteria (Optional)
Purpose – Easy to see what the site is about.
Engaging – Makes you want to explore more.
Spelling – No big spelling or grammar mistakes.
Score (0–3): 3
Feedback:
“The purpose and content of your website is very clear (baked goods recipes). The images, titles, and subheadings are engaging due to their font, style, and colour. The spelling and grammar is accurate, so the website is easy to read and follow.”





